    "UIName": "Izula II MBT",
    "Id": "vehicledef_IZULA_PRIMITIVE_2",
    "Name": "Izula II MBT",
    "Details": "Randal Advanced Tactical's Izula 2 is not a very impressive tank viewed on it's merits. Though it is a significant upgrade over the original while remaining simple and cheap. Manufacturing one requires only basic industrialization, and many of the parts can be bought off the shelf on developed worlds. This means that virtually anyone who is anyone can field a RAT. And out on the periphery any armor is better than none. In keeping with this DIY approach to defense RAT sells the plans and offers technical consultants, but doesn't manufacture the tanks themselves. This business model has been surprisingly successful.\n\n<b><color=#ffcc00>Biome Restrictions: This unit can not deploy in Lunar or Martian biomes due to using an ICE.</color></b>\n\n<b><color=#ffcc00>Movement: 4/6 hexes / 120/180 meters.</color></b>\n\n<color=#ffcc00><b>Armor:</b> Armor\n<b>Structure:</b> Structure\n<b>Values       A        S  </b>\n<b>Front</b>       190     25\n<b>Left</b>         150     25\n<b>Right</b>       150     25\n<b>Rear</b>        100     25\n<b>Turret</b>      150     25\n\n<b>Total</b>      740    125</color>\n\n<color=#ff0000>Quirk: Main Battle Tank</color>",
    "Icon": "Crusader"
  },
